      "blind_answer": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "IE1 of Pb (about 715 kJ/mol) is higher than Sn (about 708 kJ/mol), due to lanthanide contraction and poor f shielding, so I is true. S has a more negative electron gain enthalpy than O because O is small and suffers electron repulsion, so II is true."
